\* NOTE: This specification was generated by AI inference from source code. It
\* is intended only to demonstrate the feasibility of trace validation and
\* end-to-end proofs for a production Raft library. It is not an official or
\* maintained specification of etcd-io/raft, and library maintainers and users
\* should not rely on it as is.

---- MODULE EtcdRaft ----
\* Raft as etcd-io/raft implements it, in small steps, for proof. One action is
\* one step seen at raft's boundary: one change of a node's disk, one message
\* that may be sent, or one in-memory step of a leader that others can depend on.
\* Raft's single write of HardState and entries is several actions in a row;
\* every prefix is a state of the model, so the model allows more than the code.
\*
\* currentTerm, voteTerm, voteFor, log and commitIndex are what node i has ON
\* DISK. Nothing fixes when a node writes, so the synchronous Ready loop and
\* AsyncStorageWrites are both behaviours of the model:
\*  - ledLog[t] is the in-memory log of the leader of term t. LeaderAppend adds
\*    to it, SendAppend sends from it. The leader's disk gets entries by a
\*    request to itself (StoreEntries), and the leader counts in a quorum only
\*    by its own Ack (raft: MsgAppResp to itself).
\*  - A commit is a fact about a leader log (LeaderCommit); a commit index on
\*    disk moves only by FollowerCommit, the leader's own included.
\*  - Apply hands over any committed entry of the log, whatever the commit
\*    index on disk says (AsyncStorageWrites applies before that write is done).
\*  - Votes, grants, acknowledgements and vote requests are made from disk (for
\*    vote requests this is raft with patch E1, see ../patches/README.md).
\*
\* Messages are facts: msgs only grows, and any fact can be acted on at any
\* later time, any number of times (delay, loss, duplication, reordering).
\* Nodes start with an empty log at term 0; a cluster bootstrapped with a first
\* entry is the state after a first election (EtcdBinding.tla).
\*
\* Membership. Nodes start with the voters InitVoters. A "conf" entry
\* (ConfChange, ConfChangeV2) takes effect when the node applies it and calls
\* ApplyConfChange: SwitchConf. config[i] is in memory; after a restart it is
\* the snapshot's (RestoreConf) or the first one. Rules that keep two leaders
\* from counting with configurations that share no voter:
\*  - a leader appends a change only when it has switched to every change in
\*    its log (LeaderAppend; raft's pendingConfIndex);
\*  - a node becomes leader only if at most one change in its log is not
\*    switched to (BecomeLeader). Raft refuses to campaign with a committed,
\*    unapplied change, and with patch E3 knows all changes but the last to be
\*    committed;
\*  - a change that is not joint adds or removes one voter (Legal);
\*  - a node becomes leader, and a leader switches, only with changes committed
\*    under its own term or an earlier one (BecomeLeader, SwitchConf).
\* With InitVoters = Server and no "conf" entry this is fixed membership.
\*
\* Not modelled: PreVote, CheckQuorum, leadership transfer (they change nothing
\* here; the binding follows them) and learners.
\*
\* Unlike hashicorp/raft: a vote is one write (CastVote; HardState.Vote is
\* voteFor[i] if voteTerm[i] = currentTerm[i], else none); the commit index is
\* durable; a heartbeat is SendAppend with p = n = 0; a request below the
\* follower's commit index is answered with it (AckCommitted); a snapshot sent
\* is a request with the whole committed prefix (p = 0, c = n), and Restore is
\* what a snapshot does to a state machine.
\*
\* `confirmed` is ghost state: raft's follower commit bound (last entry of the
\* request, or the leader's match index on a heartbeat) lies within it.
\*
\* Read index (ReadIndex, ReadOnlySafe): `read` follows one read index, any
\* one, so what is proved holds of every read. Only ReadRequest, ReadAck and
\* ReadConfirm change it, and they change nothing else. ReadIndexSafety: when
\* the read may be served, its index covers every prefix committed when it was
\* asked for; with CommitSafety and StateMachineSafety the read is
\* linearizable. Proved in ../veil and proof/. EtcdBinding.tla checks it on
\* every read (ReadGiven) but does not replay these actions.
\* Argument: a prefix committed at the request was acknowledged to the leader
\* of some term by a quorum. Were that term after the reader's, that quorum (in
\* a configuration at most one change from the reader's) would share a node
\* with the read's answerers, none of which acknowledged in a later term.
EXTENDS Naturals, FiniteSets, Sequences

CONSTANTS Server,      \* every node that is ever part of the cluster
          InitVoters,  \* the voters every node starts with
          Values,      \* client command payloads
          Nil          \* "no server" / "no value"

ASSUME Nil \notin Server
\* Named assumptions, cited by the proofs. Server is finite (quorums are counted).
ASSUME VotersOK == InitVoters \subseteq Server /\ InitVoters # {}
ASSUME ServerFinite == IsFiniteSet(Server)

Follower  == "follower"
Candidate == "candidate"
Leader    == "leader"

VARIABLES
    \* On disk. Node i's last vote was for voteFor[i] in term voteTerm[i].
    currentTerm, voteTerm, voteFor, log, commitIndex,
    \* Volatile. lastApplied[i]: entries handed to the state machine since start.
    role, lastApplied,
    \* Volatile. config[i] = [in, out]: the voters i counts with, and inside a
    \* joint change the voters before it ({} otherwise). confAt[i]: index of the
    \* entry that made it (0: InitConf).
    config, confAt,
    \* confirmed[i] = [term, index]: the first `index` entries of log[i] are
    \* those of the leader log of `term`.
    confirmed,
    \* Facts: msgs sent; votes (voter, term, cand) ever held; leaders (server, term).
    msgs, votes, leaders,
    \* ledLog[t]: in-memory log of the leader of term t (frozen when it stops).
    \* Starts as that node's disk log and only grows.
    ledLog,
    \* ledConf[t]: that leader's configuration; ledAt[t]: index of the entry of
    \* ledLog[t] that made it (0: none); elAt[t]: the same at election.
    ledConf, ledAt, elAt,
    \* History: every committed prefix observed, by a leader of its leader log
    \* (LeaderCommit) or by a node of its own log (FollowerCommit).
    commits,
    \* History: every (server, index, entry) handed to a state machine.
    applied,
    \* The followed read index: on, done (may be served), leader term, index,
    \* commits and msgs when asked (floor, msgs), and who answered (resp).
    read

durable  == <<currentTerm, voteTerm, voteFor, log, commitIndex>>
protoVars == <<currentTerm, voteTerm, voteFor, log, commitIndex, role, lastApplied,
               config, confAt, confirmed, msgs, votes, leaders, ledLog, ledConf, ledAt, elAt>>
\* The protocol and its history; `read` apart.
vars == <<protoVars, commits, applied>>
rvars == <<vars, read>>

Min(a, b) == IF a <= b THEN a ELSE b
Max(a, b) == IF a >= b THEN a ELSE b
Majority(S, V) == Cardinality(S \cap V) * 2 > Cardinality(V)
\* S is a quorum of C: a majority of C.in, and of C.out if C is joint.
IsQuorum(S, C) == Majority(S, C.in) /\ (C.out = {} \/ Majority(S, C.out))
IsPrefix(a, b) == Len(a) <= Len(b) /\ a = SubSeq(b, 1, Len(a))
TermAt(l, k) == IF k > 0 /\ k <= Len(l) THEN l[k].term ELSE 0
LastTerm(i) == TermAt(log[i], Len(log[i]))
Entry(t, ty, v) == [term |-> t, type |-> ty, value |-> v]

----
\* A "conf" entry's value is [add, remove, joint, leave] (raft's ConfChangeV2;
\* leave: the empty change that leaves a joint configuration).
Range(s) == {s[k] : k \in DOMAIN s}
IsConf(e) == e.type = "conf"
InitConf == [in |-> InitVoters, out |-> {}]

Target(C, d) == (C.in \cup Range(d.add)) \ Range(d.remove)

\* What change d makes of configuration C.
NextConf(C, d) ==
    IF d.leave THEN [in |-> C.in, out |-> {}]
    ELSE [in |-> Target(C, d), out |-> IF d.joint THEN C.in ELSE {}]

\* confchange.Changer accepts d on C (otherwise raft panics): only a joint
\* configuration is left, only a non-joint one changed, some voter remains, and
\* a non-joint change adds or removes at most one voter.
Legal(C, d) ==
    IF d.leave THEN C.out # {}
    ELSE /\ C.out = {}
         /\ Target(C, d) # {}
         /\ d.joint \/ Cardinality((C.in \ Target(C, d)) \cup (Target(C, d) \ C.in)) <= 1

\* Indexes of the changes among the first a entries of l, the last of them (0
\* for none), and the configuration they make.
ConfIdx(l, a) == {k \in 1..a : IsConf(l[k])}
LastConf(l, a) == LET S == ConfIdx(l, a) IN IF S = {} THEN 0 ELSE CHOOSE k \in S : \A q \in S : q <= k
\* A recursive function rather than RECURSIVE, which TLAPS does not handle.
ConfOf(l, a) ==
    LET f[k \in 0..a] ==
            IF k = 0 THEN InitConf
            ELSE IF IsConf(l[k]) THEN NextConf(f[k - 1], l[k].value)
            ELSE f[k - 1]
    IN f[a]

\* The changes in log l after index a.
ConfsAfter(l, a) == {k \in (a + 1)..Len(l) : IsConf(l[k])}

\* Node i has switched to every change in l / to all but at most one.
AllSwitched(i, l) == ConfsAfter(l, confAt[i]) = {}
OneWaiting(i, l) == Cardinality(ConfsAfter(l, confAt[i])) <= 1

\* No read index is followed.
NoRead == [on |-> FALSE, done |-> FALSE, term |-> 0, index |-> 0,
           floor |-> {}, msgs |-> {}, resp |-> {}]

Init ==
    /\ currentTerm = [s \in Server |-> 0]
    /\ voteTerm    = [s \in Server |-> 0]
    /\ voteFor     = [s \in Server |-> Nil]
    /\ log         = [s \in Server |-> <<>>]
    /\ role        = [s \in Server |-> Follower]
    /\ commitIndex = [s \in Server |-> 0]
    /\ lastApplied = [s \in Server |-> 0]
    /\ config      = [s \in Server |-> InitConf]
    /\ confAt      = [s \in Server |-> 0]
    /\ confirmed   = [s \in Server |-> [term |-> 0, index |-> 0]]
    /\ msgs        = {}
    /\ votes       = {}
    /\ leaders     = {}
    /\ ledLog      = <<>>
    /\ ledConf     = <<>>
    /\ ledAt       = <<>>
    /\ elAt        = <<>>
    /\ commits     = {}
    /\ applied     = {}
    /\ read        = NoRead

----
\* Roles.

BecomeCandidate(i) ==
    /\ role' = [role EXCEPT ![i] = Candidate]
    /\ UNCHANGED <<durable, lastApplied, config, confAt, confirmed, msgs, votes, leaders, ledLog, ledConf, ledAt, elAt, commits, applied>>

BecomeFollower(i) ==
    /\ role' = [role EXCEPT ![i] = Follower]
    /\ UNCHANGED <<durable, lastApplied, config, confAt, confirmed, msgs, votes, leaders, ledLog, ledConf, ledAt, elAt, commits, applied>>

----
\* Terms and votes.

VoteRequest(i, t) ==
    [type |-> "vote", src |-> i, term |-> t,
     lastLogIndex |-> Len(log[i]), lastLogTerm |-> LastTerm(i)]

\* becomeCandidate and campaign: next term, and the vote request becomes a fact.
\* (raft's self-vote in the same write is CastVote(i, i).)
StartElection(i) ==
    /\ role[i] = Candidate
    /\ currentTerm' = [currentTerm EXCEPT ![i] = @ + 1]
    /\ msgs' = msgs \cup {VoteRequest(i, currentTerm[i] + 1)}
    /\ UNCHANGED <<voteTerm, voteFor, log, commitIndex, role, lastApplied, config, confAt, confirmed, votes, leaders, ledLog, ledConf, ledAt, elAt, commits, applied>>

\* Adopt a later term some other node has reached, as a follower.
AdoptTerm(i, t) ==
    /\ t > currentTerm[i]
    /\ \E k \in Server \ {i} : currentTerm[k] >= t
    /\ currentTerm' = [currentTerm EXCEPT ![i] = t]
    /\ role' = [role EXCEPT ![i] = Follower]
    /\ UNCHANGED <<voteTerm, voteFor, log, commitIndex, lastApplied, config, confAt, confirmed, msgs, votes, leaders, ledLog, ledConf, ledAt, elAt, commits, applied>>

UpToDate(m, i) ==
    \/ m.lastLogTerm > LastTerm(i)
    \/ m.lastLogTerm = LastTerm(i) /\ m.lastLogIndex >= Len(log[i])

\* c asked for i's vote in i's term and its log is not behind i's. Covers a
\* self-vote: campaign makes the request a fact before voting.
MayVote(i, c) ==
    \E m \in msgs :
        /\ m.type = "vote" /\ m.src = c /\ m.term = currentTerm[i]
        /\ UpToDate(m, i)

\* A node that has not voted in its term votes: one write.
CastVote(i, c) ==
    /\ voteTerm[i] # currentTerm[i]
    /\ MayVote(i, c)
    /\ voteTerm' = [voteTerm EXCEPT ![i] = currentTerm[i]]
    /\ voteFor' = [voteFor EXCEPT ![i] = c]
    /\ votes' = votes \cup {[voter |-> i, term |-> currentTerm[i], cand |-> c]}
    /\ UNCHANGED <<currentTerm, log, commitIndex, role, lastApplied, config, confAt, confirmed, msgs, leaders, ledLog, ledConf, ledAt, elAt, commits, applied>>

\* A granted reply states a vote the node holds or held.
GrantVote(i, c, t) ==
    /\ c # i
    /\ [voter |-> i, term |-> t, cand |-> c] \in votes
    /\ msgs' = msgs \cup {[type |-> "grant", src |-> i, dst |-> c, term |-> t]}
    /\ UNCHANGED <<durable, role, lastApplied, config, confAt, confirmed, votes, leaders, ledLog, ledConf, ledAt, elAt, commits, applied>>

\* ledLog / ledConf / f with term t set.
WithLed(t, l) == [u \in DOMAIN ledLog \cup {t} |-> IF u = t THEN l ELSE ledLog[u]]
WithConf(t, C) == [u \in DOMAIN ledConf \cup {t} |-> IF u = t THEN C ELSE ledConf[u]]
With(f, t, k) == [u \in DOMAIN f \cup {t} |-> IF u = t THEN k ELSE f[u]]

\* The first c entries of l are committed under a term before t.
CommittedBefore(l, c, t) ==
    \/ c = 0
    \/ /\ c <= Len(l)
       /\ \E k \in commits : /\ k.term < t
                             /\ c <= Len(k.entries)
                             /\ SubSeq(k.entries, 1, c) = SubSeq(l, 1, c)

Granted(i) ==
    {j \in Server \ {i} :
        [type |-> "grant", src |-> j, dst |-> i, term |-> currentTerm[i]] \in msgs}
    \cup (IF [voter |-> i, term |-> currentTerm[i], cand |-> i] \in votes THEN {i} ELSE {})

\* A candidate with a quorum of votes leads its term, once (a leader that
\* stopped leads again only in a later term); its leader log starts as its disk
\* log. The last two conjuncts are membership rules (header).
BecomeLeader(i) ==
    /\ role[i] = Candidate
    /\ currentTerm[i] \notin DOMAIN ledLog
    /\ IsQuorum(Granted(i), config[i])
    /\ OneWaiting(i, log[i])
    /\ CommittedBefore(log[i], confAt[i], currentTerm[i])
    /\ role' = [role EXCEPT ![i] = Leader]
    /\ leaders' = leaders \cup {[server |-> i, term |-> currentTerm[i]]}
    /\ ledLog' = WithLed(currentTerm[i], log[i])
    /\ ledConf' = WithConf(currentTerm[i], config[i])
    /\ ledAt' = With(ledAt, currentTerm[i], confAt[i])
    /\ elAt' = With(elAt, currentTerm[i], confAt[i])
    /\ UNCHANGED <<durable, lastApplied, config, confAt, confirmed, msgs, votes, commits, applied>>

----
\* Leader.

\* appendEntry: entries of the leader's term, in memory (disk by StoreEntries).
\* A change only if every change in the log is switched to and it is Legal
\* (stepLeader otherwise appends an empty entry instead).
LeaderAppend(i, es) ==
    /\ role[i] = Leader
    /\ currentTerm[i] \in DOMAIN ledLog
    /\ Len(es) > 0
    /\ \A k \in 1..Len(es) : es[k].term = currentTerm[i]
    /\ \A k \in 1..Len(es) : IsConf(es[k]) =>
          /\ AllSwitched(i, ledLog[currentTerm[i]])
          /\ \A q \in 1..(k - 1) : ~IsConf(es[q])
          /\ Legal(config[i], es[k].value)
    /\ ledLog' = WithLed(currentTerm[i], ledLog[currentTerm[i]] \o es)
    /\ UNCHANGED <<durable, role, lastApplied, config, confAt, confirmed, msgs, votes, leaders, ledConf, ledAt, elAt, commits, applied>>

\* A committed prefix a request of term t may rely on: recorded under term t or
\* earlier (the leader's commit index was reached by then).
KnownIn(k, t) == k.term <= t

\* The first c entries of l are committed, as far as term t knows.
CommittedIn(l, c, t) ==
    \/ c = 0
    \/ /\ c <= Len(l)
       /\ \E k \in commits : /\ KnownIn(k, t)
                             /\ c <= Len(k.entries)
                             /\ SubSeq(k.entries, 1, c) = SubSeq(l, 1, c)

\* maybeSendAppend (sendHeartbeat: p = n = 0): a request of term t from its
\* leader, n entries after index p of ledLog[t], commit index committed as
\* term t knows. Independent of the sender's current state; j = i is the
\* leader's write to its own disk.
SendAppend(i, j, t, p, n, c) ==
    /\ [server |-> i, term |-> t] \in leaders
    /\ p + n <= Len(ledLog[t])
    /\ CommittedIn(ledLog[t], c, t)
    /\ msgs' = msgs \cup {[type |-> "append", src |-> i, dst |-> j, term |-> t,
                           prevLogIndex |-> p, prevLogTerm |-> TermAt(ledLog[t], p),
                           entries |-> SubSeq(ledLog[t], p + 1, p + n), commit |-> c]}
    /\ UNCHANGED <<durable, role, lastApplied, config, confAt, confirmed, votes, leaders, ledLog, ledConf, ledAt, elAt, commits, applied>>

\* Nodes that acknowledged the first c entries to i, leader of term t (i only
\* by its own ack).
Acked(i, t, c) ==
    {j \in Server :
        \E a \in msgs : /\ a.type = "ack" /\ a.src = j /\ a.dst = i
                        /\ a.term = t /\ a.index >= c}

Committed(s, t, c) == [server |-> s, term |-> t, entries |-> SubSeq(log[s], 1, c)]

\* The leader of t sees a quorum of its configuration hold an entry of term t:
\* the prefix of its leader log is recorded as committed. Its own disk and
\* role are not involved; its commit index moves by FollowerCommit.
LeaderCommit(i, t, c) ==
    /\ [server |-> i, term |-> t] \in leaders
    /\ c >= 1
    /\ c <= Len(ledLog[t])
    /\ ledLog[t][c].term = t
    /\ IsQuorum(Acked(i, t, c), ledConf[t])
    /\ commits' = commits \cup {[server |-> i, term |-> t, entries |-> SubSeq(ledLog[t], 1, c)]}
    /\ UNCHANGED <<durable, role, lastApplied, config, confAt, confirmed, msgs, votes, leaders, ledLog, ledConf, ledAt, elAt, applied>>

----
\* Follower, given an append request m addressed to it.

PrevOk(j, m) ==
    IF m.prevLogIndex = 0 THEN TRUE
    ELSE /\ m.prevLogIndex <= Len(log[j])
         /\ log[j][m.prevLogIndex].term = m.prevLogTerm

\* The first k entries of m are in j's log where m puts them.
HasFirst(j, m, k) ==
    \A q \in 1..k :
        /\ m.prevLogIndex + q <= Len(log[j])
        /\ log[j][m.prevLogIndex + q].term = m.entries[q].term

Confirm(j, t, k) == [confirmed EXCEPT ![j] = [term |-> t, index |-> k]]

\* maybeAppend: delete the suffix from the first conflict.
DeleteSuffix(j, m, k) ==
    /\ m \in msgs /\ m.type = "append" /\ m.dst = j
    /\ m.term = currentTerm[j]
    /\ PrevOk(j, m)
    /\ k \in 1..Len(m.entries)
    /\ HasFirst(j, m, k - 1)
    /\ m.prevLogIndex + k <= Len(log[j])
    /\ log[j][m.prevLogIndex + k].term # m.entries[k].term
    /\ log' = [log EXCEPT ![j] = SubSeq(@, 1, m.prevLogIndex + k - 1)]
    /\ confirmed' = Confirm(j, m.term, m.prevLogIndex + k - 1)
    /\ UNCHANGED <<currentTerm, voteTerm, voteFor, commitIndex, role, lastApplied, config, confAt, msgs, votes, leaders, ledLog, ledConf, ledAt, elAt, commits, applied>>

\* maybeAppend: store the entries of m from the k-th on, at the end of the log.
StoreEntries(j, m, k) ==
    /\ m \in msgs /\ m.type = "append" /\ m.dst = j
    /\ m.term = currentTerm[j]
    /\ PrevOk(j, m)
    /\ k \in 1..Len(m.entries)
    /\ HasFirst(j, m, k - 1)
    /\ m.prevLogIndex + k = Len(log[j]) + 1
    /\ log' = [log EXCEPT ![j] = @ \o SubSeq(m.entries, k, Len(m.entries))]
    /\ confirmed' = Confirm(j, m.term, m.prevLogIndex + Len(m.entries))
    /\ UNCHANGED <<currentTerm, voteTerm, voteFor, commitIndex, role, lastApplied, config, confAt, msgs, votes, leaders, ledLog, ledConf, ledAt, elAt, commits, applied>>

\* Successful reply: j's log holds all of m. Only in m's term: a node in a later
\* term may have voted for a candidate lacking these entries, or hold them only
\* from a later leader.
Ack(j, m) ==
    /\ m \in msgs /\ m.type = "append" /\ m.dst = j
    /\ currentTerm[j] = m.term
    /\ PrevOk(j, m)
    /\ HasFirst(j, m, Len(m.entries))
    /\ LET last == m.prevLogIndex + Len(m.entries)
       IN /\ msgs' = msgs \cup {[type |-> "ack", src |-> j, dst |-> m.src,
                                 term |-> m.term, index |-> last]}
          /\ confirmed' = Confirm(j, m.term,
                                  IF confirmed[j].term = m.term
                                  THEN Max(confirmed[j].index, last) ELSE last)
    /\ UNCHANGED <<durable, role, lastApplied, config, confAt, votes, leaders, ledLog, ledConf, ledAt, elAt, commits, applied>>

\* handleAppendEntries, first branch: a request below j's commit index is
\* answered with the commit index (sound: m.term's leader has every entry
\* committed before or in its term). Nothing compared, nothing confirmed.
AckCommitted(j, m) ==
    /\ m \in msgs /\ m.type = "append" /\ m.dst = j
    /\ currentTerm[j] = m.term
    /\ m.prevLogIndex < commitIndex[j]
    /\ msgs' = msgs \cup {[type |-> "ack", src |-> j, dst |-> m.src,
                            term |-> m.term, index |-> commitIndex[j]]}
    /\ UNCHANGED <<durable, role, lastApplied, config, confAt, confirmed, votes, leaders, ledLog, ledConf, ledAt, elAt, commits, applied>>

\* Commit up to the leader's commit index, within what this leader confirmed.
FollowerCommit(j, m, c) ==
    /\ m \in msgs /\ m.type = "append" /\ m.dst = j
    /\ m.term = confirmed[j].term
    /\ c > commitIndex[j]
    /\ c <= Min(m.commit, confirmed[j].index)
    /\ commitIndex' = [commitIndex EXCEPT ![j] = c]
    /\ commits' = commits \cup {Committed(j, m.term, c)}
    /\ UNCHANGED <<currentTerm, voteTerm, voteFor, log, role, lastApplied, config, confAt, confirmed, msgs, votes, leaders, ledLog, ledConf, ledAt, elAt, applied>>

----
\* Hand the next entry to the state machine if some recorded committed prefix
\* has it; the node's own commit index is not consulted (AsyncStorageWrites).
IsCommitted(l, k) ==
    \E c \in commits : k <= Len(c.entries) /\ SubSeq(c.entries, 1, k) = SubSeq(l, 1, k)

Apply(i) ==
    LET k == lastApplied[i] + 1 IN
    /\ k <= Len(log[i])
    /\ IsCommitted(log[i], k)
    /\ lastApplied' = [lastApplied EXCEPT ![i] = k]
    /\ applied' = applied \cup {[server |-> i, index |-> k, entry |-> log[i][k]]}
    /\ UNCHANGED <<durable, role, config, confAt, confirmed, msgs, votes, leaders, ledLog, ledConf, ledAt, elAt, commits>>

----
\* Restart: durable state, commit index included, survives; the state machine
\* starts empty and is handed the log again.
Restart(i) ==
    /\ role' = [role EXCEPT ![i] = Follower]
    /\ lastApplied' = [lastApplied EXCEPT ![i] = 0]
    /\ config' = [config EXCEPT ![i] = InitConf]
    /\ confAt' = [confAt EXCEPT ![i] = 0]
    /\ UNCHANGED <<durable, confirmed, msgs, votes, leaders, ledLog, ledConf, ledAt, elAt, commits, applied>>

\* The state machine is replaced by one that applied a committed prefix of
\* the log (a snapshot of its own or from a leader; a = 0: empty). Nothing is
\* added to applied.
Restore(i, a) ==
    /\ a \in 0..Len(log[i])
    /\ a = 0 \/ IsCommitted(log[i], a)
    /\ lastApplied' = [lastApplied EXCEPT ![i] = a]
    /\ UNCHANGED <<durable, role, config, confAt, confirmed, msgs, votes, leaders, ledLog, ledConf, ledAt, elAt, commits, applied>>

\* A non-leader takes the ConfState of a snapshot: the configuration of the
\* first a entries of a committed prefix. Raft does so on receipt, before
\* writing it, so neither log nor lastApplied is checked (BecomeLeader checks
\* the log).
RestoreConf(i, c, a) ==
    /\ c \in commits /\ a \in 0..Len(c.entries)
    /\ role[i] # Leader
    /\ config' = [config EXCEPT ![i] = ConfOf(c.entries, a)]
    /\ confAt' = [confAt EXCEPT ![i] = LastConf(c.entries, a)]
    /\ UNCHANGED <<durable, role, lastApplied, confirmed, msgs, votes, leaders, ledLog, ledConf, ledAt, elAt, commits, applied>>

\* Leader i knows its first k entries committed under its term or earlier.
LeaderKnows(i, k) == CommittedIn(log[i], k, currentTerm[i])

\* ApplyConfChange: the node applied the next change in its log and counts
\* with the new configuration. A leader must know it committed in its term or
\* earlier.
SwitchConf(i, k) ==
    /\ k > confAt[i] /\ k <= lastApplied[i] /\ k <= Len(log[i])
    /\ IsCommitted(log[i], k)
    /\ IsConf(log[i][k])
    /\ \A q \in (confAt[i] + 1)..(k - 1) : ~IsConf(log[i][q])
    /\ Legal(config[i], log[i][k].value)
    /\ role[i] = Leader => LeaderKnows(i, k)
    /\ LET C == NextConf(config[i], log[i][k].value) IN
       /\ config' = [config EXCEPT ![i] = C]
       /\ ledConf' = IF role[i] = Leader THEN WithConf(currentTerm[i], C) ELSE ledConf
    /\ ledAt' = IF role[i] = Leader THEN With(ledAt, currentTerm[i], k) ELSE ledAt
    /\ confAt' = [confAt EXCEPT ![i] = k]
    /\ UNCHANGED <<durable, role, lastApplied, confirmed, msgs, votes, leaders, ledLog, elAt, commits, applied>>

----
\* Every change among nodes N (add/remove: sequences without repeats).
Seqs(N) ==
    UNION {{s \in [1..n -> N] : \A p, q \in 1..n : p # q => s[p] # s[q]}
           : n \in 0..Cardinality(N)}
ConfChanges(N) ==
    {[add |-> a, remove |-> r, joint |-> j, leave |-> FALSE] : a \in Seqs(N), r \in Seqs(N), j \in BOOLEAN}
    \cup {[add |-> <<>>, remove |-> <<>>, joint |-> FALSE, leave |-> TRUE]}

ProtoNext ==
    \/ \E i \in Server :
          \/ BecomeCandidate(i) \/ BecomeFollower(i) \/ BecomeLeader(i)
          \/ StartElection(i) \/ Restart(i) \/ Apply(i)
          \/ \E a \in 0..Len(log[i]) : Restore(i, a)
          \/ \E k \in 1..Len(log[i]) : SwitchConf(i, k)
          \/ \E c \in commits : \E a \in 0..Len(c.entries) : RestoreConf(i, c, a)
          \/ \E d \in ConfChanges(Server) : LeaderAppend(i, <<Entry(currentTerm[i], "conf", d)>>)
          \/ \E t \in {currentTerm[k] : k \in Server} : AdoptTerm(i, t)
          \/ \E c \in Server : CastVote(i, c)
          \/ \E v \in votes : v.voter = i /\ GrantVote(i, v.cand, v.term)
          \/ \E ty \in {"noop", "config"} : LeaderAppend(i, <<Entry(currentTerm[i], ty, Nil)>>)
          \/ \E v \in Values : LeaderAppend(i, <<Entry(currentTerm[i], "command", v)>>)
          \/ \E l \in leaders : l.server = i /\ \E c \in 1..Len(ledLog[l.term]) : LeaderCommit(i, l.term, c)
          \/ \E j \in Server, l \in leaders :
                /\ l.server = i
                /\ \E p, n, c \in 0..Len(ledLog[l.term]) : SendAppend(i, j, l.term, p, n, c)
    \/ \E m \in msgs :
          /\ m.type = "append"
          /\ \/ Ack(m.dst, m) \/ AckCommitted(m.dst, m)
             \/ \E k \in 1..Len(m.entries) : DeleteSuffix(m.dst, m, k) \/ StoreEntries(m.dst, m, k)
             \/ \E c \in 1..m.commit : FollowerCommit(m.dst, m, c)

----
\* Read index actions; they change only `read`.

\* A leader that has committed an entry of its term gives an index covering
\* every prefix committed under its term or earlier.
ReadRequest(i, c) ==
    /\ role[i] = Leader
    /\ LET t == currentTerm[i] IN
       /\ t \in DOMAIN ledLog /\ c <= Len(ledLog[t])
       /\ \E k \in commits : k.term = t
       /\ \A k \in commits : k.term <= t => Len(k.entries) <= c
       /\ read' = [on |-> TRUE, done |-> FALSE, term |-> t, index |-> c,
                   floor |-> commits, msgs |-> msgs, resp |-> {}]
    /\ UNCHANGED vars

\* j answers the read's heartbeat: its disk is not in a later term (raft: it is
\* in the leader's term in memory, and its disk is never ahead of that).
ReadAck(j) ==
    /\ read.on /\ currentTerm[j] <= read.term
    /\ read' = [read EXCEPT !.resp = @ \cup {j}]
    /\ UNCHANGED vars

\* Quorum of the leader's current configuration (readOnly.recvAck).
ReadConfirm ==
    /\ read.on /\ IsQuorum(read.resp, ledConf[read.term])
    /\ read' = [read EXCEPT !.done = TRUE]
    /\ UNCHANGED vars

ReadNext ==
    \/ \E i \in Server :
          \/ ReadAck(i)
          \/ /\ role[i] = Leader /\ currentTerm[i] \in DOMAIN ledLog
             /\ \E c \in 0..Len(ledLog[currentTerm[i]]) : ReadRequest(i, c)
    \/ ReadConfirm

\* Modules with their own next-state relation (binding, bounded instances)
\* add UNCHANGED read.
Next == (ProtoNext /\ UNCHANGED read) \/ ReadNext
Spec == Init /\ [][Next]_rvars

----
\* Safety properties.

\* At most one server is elected in a term.
ElectionSafety ==
    \A a, b \in leaders : a.term = b.term => a.server = b.server

\* A node never votes for two candidates in one term.
OneVotePerTerm ==
    \A a, b \in votes : a.voter = b.voter /\ a.term = b.term => a.cand = b.cand

\* Equal terms at an index imply equal prefixes.
LogMatching ==
    \A a, b \in Server :
        \A k \in 1..Min(Len(log[a]), Len(log[b])) :
            log[a][k].term = log[b][k].term =>
                SubSeq(log[a], 1, k) = SubSeq(log[b], 1, k)

\* Two committed prefixes never disagree.
CommitSafety ==
    \A a, b \in commits : IsPrefix(a.entries, b.entries) \/ IsPrefix(b.entries, a.entries)

\* No two state machines are ever handed different entries at one index
\* (nor is one state machine, before and after a restart).
StateMachineSafety ==
    \A a, b \in applied : a.index = b.index => a.entry = b.entry

\* The leader log of a term has every prefix committed under an earlier
\* term.
LeaderCompleteness ==
    \A t \in DOMAIN ledLog, c \in commits :
        c.term < t => IsPrefix(c.entries, ledLog[t])

\* The first commitIndex[i] entries of log[i] start a committed prefix
\* recorded under i's name.
CommittedEntriesPreserved ==
    \A i \in Server :
        /\ commitIndex[i] <= Len(log[i])
        /\ commitIndex[i] = 0 \/
             \E c \in commits : /\ c.server = i
                                /\ IsPrefix(SubSeq(log[i], 1, commitIndex[i]), c.entries)

\* Invariants the proofs use. A leader's disk log is a prefix of its leader log.
LeaderLogIsLed ==
    \A i \in Server : role[i] = Leader =>
        /\ currentTerm[i] \in DOMAIN ledLog
        /\ IsPrefix(log[i], ledLog[currentTerm[i]])

\* What a leader has confirmed of a node's log is in that log.
ConfirmedWithinLog ==
    \A i \in Server : confirmed[i].index <= Len(log[i])

\* A request carries a segment of its term's leader log and a committed commit index.
RequestsFromLed ==
    \A m \in msgs : m.type = "append" =>
        /\ m.term \in DOMAIN ledLog
        /\ m.prevLogIndex + Len(m.entries) <= Len(ledLog[m.term])
        /\ m.prevLogTerm = TermAt(ledLog[m.term], m.prevLogIndex)
        /\ m.entries = SubSeq(ledLog[m.term], m.prevLogIndex + 1, m.prevLogIndex + Len(m.entries))
        /\ CommittedIn(ledLog[m.term], m.commit, m.term)

\* A node's configuration is that of the first confAt entries of some committed
\* prefix (not necessarily of its current log).
ConfIsCommitted ==
    \A i \in Server :
        \/ confAt[i] = 0 /\ config[i] = InitConf
        \/ \E c \in commits :
              /\ confAt[i] <= Len(c.entries)
              /\ config[i] = ConfOf(c.entries, confAt[i])

\* A leader's configuration is that of its leader log up to ledAt (at most one
\* change after it); elAt <= ledAt.
LeaderConf ==
    \A t \in DOMAIN ledLog :
        /\ t \in DOMAIN ledConf /\ t \in DOMAIN ledAt /\ t \in DOMAIN elAt
        /\ elAt[t] <= ledAt[t] /\ ledAt[t] <= Len(ledLog[t])
        /\ ledConf[t] = ConfOf(ledLog[t], ledAt[t])
        /\ Cardinality(ConfsAfter(ledLog[t], ledAt[t])) <= 1

\* When the read may be served, its index covers every prefix that was
\* committed when it was asked for.
ReadIndexSafety ==
    read.done => \A k \in read.floor : Len(k.entries) <= read.index

\* Facts the proof uses: the snapshot taken at the request is still contained,
\* and the index covers what was committed then under the reader's term or before.
ReadMsgsOld == read.on => read.msgs \subseteq msgs
ReadFloorOld == read.on => read.floor \subseteq commits
ReadFloorBound ==
    read.on => \A k \in read.floor : k.term <= read.term => Len(k.entries) <= read.index

\* A node's term and commit index never decrease.
TermMonotonic ==
    [][\A i \in Server : currentTerm'[i] >= currentTerm[i]]_vars
CommitMonotonic ==
    [][\A i \in Server : commitIndex'[i] >= commitIndex[i]]_vars

\* lastApplied moves by one with that entry applied, or jumps by Restore to a
\* committed prefix.
NoAppliesSkipped ==
    [][\A i \in Server : lastApplied'[i] > lastApplied[i] =>
          \/ /\ lastApplied'[i] = lastApplied[i] + 1
             /\ \E a \in applied' : a.server = i /\ a.index = lastApplied'[i]
          \/ /\ applied' = applied
             /\ IsCommitted(log[i], lastApplied'[i])]_vars
====
